{"name":"Café de Paris","hex":"#889944","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"café","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A coffee shop; an establishment selling coffee and sometimes other non-alcoholic beverages, simple meals or snacks, with a facility to consume them on the premises.","A small restaurant of any genre."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/caf%C3%A9"},{"term":"paris","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of pari."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paris"}],"entries":[{"title":"Café de Paris, London","blocks":[{"text":"The Café de Paris was a nightclub in the West End of London, active from 1924–41 and 1948–2020. It was located on Coventry Street, which runs between Leicester Square and Piccadilly Circus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Caf%C3%A9_de_Paris_-_London_-_08.JPG/330px-Caf%C3%A9_de_Paris_-_London_-_08.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caf%C3%A9_de_Paris%2C_London"},{"title":"Café de Paris (Monaco)","blocks":[{"text":"Café de Paris is a coffeehouse and restaurant in the Belle Époque style of the early 20th century, located in Monte Carlo next to the Casino de Monte-Carlo, on the Place du Casino, Hôtel de Paris. It is owned and managed by the Société des bains de mer de Monaco."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Caf%C3%A9_de_Paris.JPG/330px-Caf%C3%A9_de_Paris.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caf%C3%A9_de_Paris_(Monaco)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Caf%C3%A9_de_Paris_-_London_-_08.JPG/500px-Caf%C3%A9_de_Paris_-_London_-_08.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Caf%C3%A9_de_Paris_-_London_-_08.JPG/1280px-Caf